1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,499
Three hundred men. Against an army so big,

2
00:00:03,499 --> 00:00:06,812
the Bible says their camels were without number.

3
00:00:07,662 --> 00:00:09,945
And God looked at Gideon's army...

4
00:00:09,945 --> 00:00:12,027
and said it was still too many.

5
00:00:14,727 --> 00:00:17,913
For seven years, Midian stripped Israel bare.

6
00:00:17,913 --> 00:00:20,887
They came like locusts, ate every harvest,

7
00:00:20,887 --> 00:00:23,577
and left God's people hiding in caves.

8
00:00:24,427 --> 00:00:28,189
One young man was threshing wheat down in a winepress,

9
00:00:28,189 --> 00:00:31,393
hiding it from the enemy. His name was Gideon.

10
00:00:32,243 --> 00:00:35,570
The Lord is with thee, thou mighty man of valour.

11
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,078
If the Lord be with us,

12
00:00:38,078 --> 00:00:40,959
why then is all this befallen us?

13
00:00:41,809 --> 00:00:44,821
Gideon was the least in his father's house,

14
00:00:44,821 --> 00:00:47,903
from the poorest family in Manasseh. But God

15
00:00:47,903 --> 00:00:51,126
doesn't call the ready. He readies the called.

16
00:00:51,976 --> 00:00:56,337
Thirty-two thousand men answered the trumpet. And the Lord said:

17
00:00:56,337 --> 00:00:59,267
the people that are with thee are too many.

18
00:01:00,117 --> 00:01:05,460
Twenty-two thousand went home afraid. Ten thousand remained. Still... too many.

19
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:08,361
At the water, God watched how they

20
00:01:08,361 --> 00:01:11,891
drank. Three hundred lapped from their hands, eyes

21
00:01:11,891 --> 00:01:14,432
on the horizon. Those were the ones.

22
00:01:15,282 --> 00:01:18,632
That night, Gideon crept to the edge of the enemy

23
00:01:18,632 --> 00:01:21,844
camp. And he heard a soldier telling his dream.

24
00:01:22,694 --> 00:01:25,271
I dreamed a cake of barley bread

25
00:01:25,271 --> 00:01:28,654
tumbled into the host of Midian. It struck

26
00:01:28,654 --> 00:01:31,231
the tent, and the tent lay flat.

27
00:01:31,731 --> 00:01:34,222
This is nothing else save the sword of

28
00:01:34,222 --> 00:01:37,367
Gideon. Into his hand hath God delivered Midian.

29
00:01:38,217 --> 00:01:41,419
Gideon bowed down and worshipped. Then he ran

30
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:43,909
back, and gave every man a trumpet,

31
00:01:43,909 --> 00:01:46,754
an empty jar, and a torch hidden inside.

32
00:01:47,604 --> 00:01:51,429
In the middle of the night, three hundred jars shattered

33
00:01:51,429 --> 00:01:54,844
at once. Three hundred torches blazed in the dark.

34
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:58,457
The sword of the Lord, and of Gideon!

35
00:01:59,307 --> 00:02:02,311
The enemy woke in terror, turned their swords

36
00:02:02,311 --> 00:02:04,914
on each other, and fled into the night.

37
00:02:05,764 --> 00:02:10,073
Three hundred men. No plan anyone would choose. Just obedience.

38
00:02:10,573 --> 00:02:12,850
So what is God asking you to let

39
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:16,195
go of, so that when the victory comes, everyone

40
00:02:16,195 --> 00:02:19,184
knows it was Him? Tell me in the comments.

41
00:02:19,184 --> 00:02:22,173
And follow for more stories from the Book.

